{
 "about": "Shared fixture for the Bandit Codes app and the WordPress QR plugin (Bandit Codes Links). Each case has a kind, an input, ok, and a note. kind is destination, base, slug or merge. A destination case may carry campaign (source, medium, campaign, content): the 2,000-character limit counts the address after the tags are added, and the tag rules apply. A merge case carries campaign and expect: the address after the tags are merged. ok is true when the checker must accept the input, and false when it must refuse. Expected values are written by hand and never computed by either checker. Append only: add cases, never edit an existing one without telling both sides.",
